     <td><para unique="1261240">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261242">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261247">AVX</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261249">Convert one single precision floating-point value from xmm1/m32 to one signed doubleword integer in r32 using truncation.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1261251">VEX.LIG.F3.0F.W1 2C /r <superscript>1</superscript></para>
      <para unique="1261252">VCVTTSS2SI r64, xmm1/m32</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261256">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261258">V/N.E.<footnote><para unique="1261292" format="TableFootnote">For this specific instruction, VEX.W/EVEX.W in non-64 bit is ignored; the instructions behaves as if the W0 version is used.</para>
        </footnote></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261263">AVX</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1261265">Convert one single precision floating-point value from xmm1/m32 to one signed quadword integer in r64 using truncation.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1261759">EVEX.LLIG.F3.0F.W0 2C /r</para>
      <para unique="1261760">VCVTTSS2SI r32, xmm1/m32{sae}</para>
